art boot_id, issued a native reboot whose ack returned before disconnect, polled until SSH exec was available again, confirmed the boot_id changed (fresh uptime), and verified sshd was active and the module stayed unloaded (including after an explicit post-reboot modprobe attempt) with the blacklist file intact.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Captured baseline boot_id and confirmed usb_storage was not loaded on node1\",\"Wrote /etc/modprobe.d/blacklist-usb-storage.conf with `blacklist usb-storage` and `install usb-storage /bin/true`\",\"Rebuilt initramfs with `dracut -f` and verified via lsinitrd that the blacklist file is baked into /boot/initramfs-3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64.img\",\"Verified `modprobe -n -v usb-storage` resolves to /bin/true (load blocked) and module stays absent from lsmod\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, sshd active status, blacklist file content\",\"Issued `shutdown -r now` in the background so the acknowledgement returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until exec succeeded again after the reboot\",\"Verified boot_id changed and uptime reset, proving a real restart\",\"Post-restart: confirmed sshd active, usb_storage still not loaded, blacklist file persisted, and an explicit `modprobe usb-storage` attempt still failed to load the module\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"usb-storage blocked from loading now (pre-reboot)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5a876233793745f3\",\"cmd-8c9f7bafe11d4c26\"],\"summary\":\"Blacklist config written and installed as install-true trap; modprobe -n -v shows resolution to /bin/true; lsmod confirms module absent; lsinitrd confirms the config is embedded in the regenerated initramfs for the running kernel\"},{\"requirement\":\"usb-storage blocked from loading after reboot (persistence)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-cc3d22420f96407c\"],\"summary\":\"After the node restart, blacklist file is intact, modprobe -n -v still resolves to /bin/true, and an explicit modprobe usb-storage call exits 0 without the module appearing in lsmod\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory restart evidence: healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6a711f0fe557498f\"],\"summary\":\"Captured pre-restart boot_id (325732f1...), sshd active, and blacklist file present\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory restart evidence: restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-94400213fab84e54\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded `shutdown -r now` returned 'reboot acknowledged and issued' before the node dropped\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory restart evidence: node unreachable during restart, then changed boot identity confirmed\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-eb37813c21da4d73\",\"cmd-2dbe7274f88745b1\"],\"summary\":\"SSH timed out mid-restart; subsequent poll succeeded with a new boot_id (a143cc2b...) and fresh uptime timestamp, proving an actual reboot occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory restart evidence: post-restart service/data recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-cc3d22420f96407c\"],\"summary\":\"sshd active and usb-storage blacklist verified functioning identically after the restart\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Blacklisted usb-storage on node1 (RHEL7, kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7) via /etc/modprobe.d/blacklist-usb-storage.conf using both `blacklist` and `install ... /bin/true` directives, rebuilt the initramfs with dracut so the block applies at early boot, and confirmed the module cannot be loaded now or after a reboot. Completed the mandatory single-node restart/recovery protocol: captured pre-restart boot_id, issued a native reboot whose ack returned before disconnect, polled until SSH exec was available again, confirmed the boot_id changed (fresh uptime), and verified sshd was active and the module stayed unloaded (including after an explicit post-reboot modprobe attempt) with the blacklist file intact.","actions_performed":["Captured baseline boot_id and confirmed usb_storage was not loaded on node1","Wrote /etc/modprobe.d/blacklist-usb-storage.conf with `blacklist usb-storage` and `install usb-storage /bin/true`","Rebuilt initramfs with `dracut -f` and verified via lsinitrd that the blacklist file is baked into /boot/initramfs-3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64.img","Verified `modprobe -n -v usb-storage` resolves to /bin/true (load blocked) and module stays absent from lsmod","Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, sshd active status, blacklist file content","Issued `shutdown -r now` in the background so the acknowledgement returned before disconnection","Polled node1 until exec succeeded again after the reboot","Verified boot_id changed and uptime reset, proving a real restart","Post-restart: confirmed sshd active, usb_storage still not loaded, blacklist file persisted, and an explicit `modprobe usb-storage` attempt still failed to load the module"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"usb-storage blocked from loading now (pre-reboot)","command_ids":["cmd-5a876233793745f3","cmd-8c9f7bafe11d4c26"],"summary":"Blacklist config written and installed as install-true trap; modprobe -n -v shows resolution to /bin/true; lsmod confirms module absent; lsinitrd confirms the config is embedded in the regenerated initramfs for the running kernel"},{"requirement":"usb-storage blocked from loading after reboot (persistence)","command_ids":["cmd-cc3d22420f96407c"],"summary":"After the node restart, blacklist file is intact, modprobe -n -v still resolves to /bin/true, and an explicit modprobe usb-storage call exits 0 without the module appearing in lsmod"},{"requirement":"Mandatory restart evidence: healthy baseline before restart","command_ids":["cmd-6a711f0fe557498f"],"summary":"Captured pre-restart boot_id (325732f1...), sshd active, and blacklist file present"},{"requirement":"Mandatory restart evidence: restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-94400213fab84e54"],"summary":"Backgrounded `shutdown -r now` returned 'reboot acknowledged and issued' before the node dropped"},{"requirement":"Mandatory restart evidence: node unreachable during restart, then changed boot identity confirmed","command_ids":["cmd-eb37813c21da4d73","cmd-2dbe7274f88745b1"],"summary":"SSH timed out mid-restart; subsequent poll succeeded with a new boot_id (a143cc2b...) and fresh uptime timestamp, proving an actual reboot occurred"},{"requirement":"Mandatory restart evidence: post-restart service/data recovery","command_ids":["cmd-cc3d22420f96407c"],"summary":"sshd active and usb-storage blacklist verified functioning identically after the restart"}]},"ttft_ms":2193,"type":"result","duration_ms":88415,"uuid":"cfcc55de-f639-4fce-9a0d-4a95b28f0826","ttft_stream_ms":1939,"time_to_request_ms":61,"first_content_frame_ms":1940,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
